# C1-S01 / C1-S01B — Village Gate and the Road Ledger.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1502–1570.
# Scene: Oakhaven (village / region). No prophecy, no hero's welcome.
# The ledger links Kaelen's personal goal to Oakhaven's problems: he needs the
# south road, and the south road needs fixing.

~ start
Bran: Three hours, Elara. You said one.
Elara: I found a problem.
Kaelen: Hi.
Bran: Does it talk?
Elara: You'll wish it didn't.
Kaelen: We've only just met.
Bran: ...That's crater dust. You came from the north.
Elara: From the crater.
Bran: Elara.
Elara: I know.
Bran: Does Mara know?
Elara: Why would Mara know?
Bran: Mara knows everything by lunch.
Mara: I heard that!
Bran: See?
set ch1_oakhaven_entered
do gate_opens

~ ledger
Kaelen: Elara said you keep road records.
Bran: I keep the arguments written down, so everyone can have exactly the same argument again next spring. It's called civic memory. Nobody thanks me for it.
Kaelen: Has anyone else ever come out of the crater?
Bran: What, today?
Kaelen: Ever.
do bran_opens_ledger
# Mostly caravans, weather closures, missing goats, patrol notes. A few old
# entries are marked NORTHFALL.
Bran: We've found people up north before. Near it, not in it. One at a time, usually.
Kaelen: Usually?
Bran: Rare enough that we remember them, common enough that I stopped saying "impossible". The ledger calls them Northfalls.
do ledger_entry_highlight
Kaelen: This one says "transferred to Ironhold Arrival Registry".
Bran: Years back, that. Name's gone, the ink ran. Ironhold took them, whoever they were.
# This entry is Seraphina. Nobody, the player included, can know that yet.
set ch1_northfall_registry_seen
Kaelen: Then I need Ironhold.
Bran: Then you need the south road. And the south road needs the old watch route—
Elara: —which has been bad all week.
Bran: North field's worse.
Kaelen: How much worse?
Bran: You've turned up on a very educational day, lad.
do journal Lead: the Ironhold Arrival Registry. Blocker: Oakhaven's road south is unsafe.
